cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GRM-TCM Synthetic Benchmark"
message: "If you use this software or its synthetic dataset in research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Tadej
    family-names: Fius
    email: tadej.fius@gmail.com
  - given-names: Tims
    family-names: Pecerskis
repository-code: "https://github.com/tfius/grm-tcm"
license: Apache-2.0
license-url: "https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0"
keywords:
  - synthetic benchmark
  - spectral graph methods
  - latent state recovery
  - calibration
  - ontology mismatch detection
  - regime-switching state space
  - longitudinal physiology
abstract: >-
  A research prototype that adapts the Geometric Resonance Model (GRM) — a
  resolvent-style spectral graph method originally formulated for price action —
  to longitudinal physiological data. The repository ships a regime-switching
  synthetic generator with controlled ontology mismatch, plus diagnostic and
  evaluation harnesses that test latent-state recovery, attractor fingerprinting,
  and observation-aliased regime separation under subject-grouped cross-validation
  with cluster-bootstrap confidence intervals. Outputs are framed as synthetic
  benchmark diagnostics, not clinical or biological claims.
